# A descriptor with neither an executable body nor a trailer stays without an implementation as the model of
# a callable merge (T7-TRAILER-ONLY-MODEL-CRASH: it crashed the translator as a trailer-only model did).  Its
# direct call is refused as not callable (unit_callable_descriptor_direct_refused); merge(test3), invoked
# through w, has nothing to walk and is refused at the merge, not given an invented step.
fn: test3 () int
end: test3

fn: make () fn: () int
    return: merge(test3)

@: w make()
int: v (w())
int: ok 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
